  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1223 PM CDT Sat Jun 6 2026\n\nAn upper level low currently over Oklahoma will continue to trek \nnorthward into the area this evening. Showers and a few \nthunderstorms are expected across south central Kansas this \nafternoon into this evening, otherwise expect mostly cloudy skies \nthrough tonight. Clearing is then expected tomorrow as upper level \nridging builds over the Plains. Mid to upper level cloudiness then \nincreases tomorrow night with dry conditions at the surface. Winds \nwill generally be form the south to southeast through this period. \nAs for temperatures, highs this afternoon look to only reach into \nthe 80s due to the abundant cloud cover with lows tonight in the mid \n50s west to mid 60s east. Highs tomorrow will reach into the upper \n80s with 90s expected across far southwestern Kansas and along the \nKS/OK border. Lows tomorrow night will generally dip into the 60s. \n\nAn upper level trough will dig into the western United States \nthrough the remainder of the forecast with ridging to the east. THis \nwill place southwest Kansas under southwest flow aloft. A warming \ntrend is expected early next week with highs in the 90s Monday and \naround 100 degrees Tuesday and Wednesday. Dry conditions are \nexpected for a majority of this time but a stray thunderstorm or two \ncan not be ruled out during peak heating. Warm conditions continue \nfor the remainder of the forecast with highs in the 90s.",
